--- THREE Vivado crashes across THREE integration methods (conclusive) ---
  T0031  raw-RTL co-synth of all IPs        -> EXCEPTION_BREAKPOINT
  T0032  bottom-up DCP read_checkpoint-cell -> [Project 1-9] link failure
  T0034  IP-Integrator create_bd_cell       -> EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION
Every method that combines the full IP set into one Vivado design fails on
this host. Single-module operations (per-IP HLS csynth, per-IP Vivado OOC
synth, the scheduler, the rate variants) ALL succeed. The orch's T0034 note
anticipated exactly this: "If Vivado crashes again ... this strongly
implicates the 16 GB host RAM." The evidence now strongly confirms it —
integration-scale Vivado operations exceed this host's capacity / hit an
install instability.

--- bottom-up DCP fallback: also already exhausted ---
The orch directed "fall back to bottom-up DCP linking" on a crash. That was
already attempted in T0032: the 5 component DCPs synthesized fine, but
`read_checkpoint -cell` linking failed with [Project 1-9]. So the fallback
